1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:01,390
This video that you're watching right now

2
00:00:01,390 --> 00:00:03,480
has been edited entirely by Claude.

3
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:04,870
To set this up, open up Claude code

4
00:00:04,870 --> 00:00:05,880
and paste in this prompt.

5
00:00:05,880 --> 00:00:07,540
It installs a plugin called ChatCut,

6
00:00:07,540 --> 00:00:08,990
which gives Claude an actual video editing

7
00:00:08,990 --> 00:00:09,920
timeline to work with.

8
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:11,350
Once it's installed, start a new session

9
00:00:11,350 --> 00:00:12,240
and add your footage.

10
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:13,710
I'd start by asking it to remove all

11
00:00:13,710 --> 00:00:15,040
the pauses and repeated takes,

12
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:16,530
because apparently I need three attempts

13
00:00:16,530 --> 00:00:17,440
to finish a sentence.

14
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:18,920
Then you can build up the edit from there.

15
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:20,780
Ask it to add captions, find some B-roll

16
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:22,150
for what you're explaining, or bring

17
00:00:22,150 --> 00:00:23,040
in background music.

18
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:24,420
You don't have to describe the entire

19
00:00:24,420 --> 00:00:25,880
video perfectly on your first try.

20
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:27,520
You can watch the cut, see what feels off,

21
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:28,560
and ask it to change that.

22
00:00:28,590 --> 00:00:30,120
Everything is on an editable timeline.

23
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:31,200
You can also go in and move things

24
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:31,860
around yourself.

25
00:00:31,880 --> 00:00:32,970
And once you get an editing process

26
00:00:32,970 --> 00:00:34,590
that you like, you can save it as a skill

27
00:00:34,590 --> 00:00:35,730
and reuse it with your next batch

28
00:00:35,730 --> 00:00:36,380
of footage.

29
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:38,020
That's the part I'm interested in, getting

30
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:39,010
a workflow together that I can

31
00:00:39,010 --> 00:00:39,880
actually keep using.

